          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let after x years, ratio of Harmain’s age to the brother be 1 : 2 "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x + 1 : x + 5 = 1 : 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { x + 1 } { x + 5 } = \\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2x + 2 = x + 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " x = 3 Hence after 3 years Harmain’s age will be 4 years."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.23,
            0.848,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The mass of equal volumes of gold and water are in the ratio 37 : 2. If 1 litre of water is 1 kg in mass, what is the mass of 1 litre of gold?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.275,
            0.848,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "algorithm_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.151,
                0.275,
                0.848,
                0.42
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Ans. Given 1lt of water = 1 kg of its mass\nLet 1 lt of gold = x kg of its mass\nGiven the ratio of mass of equal volume of gold to water is 37 :\nSo 37 : 2 :: x : 1\nOr "
                },
                {
                  "type": "equation_inline",
                  "content": "x=\\frac{37\\times1}{2}=18.5\\  kg"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "\nHence mass of 1 litre of gold is 18.5 kg."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "sub_type": "algorithm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.427,
            0.848,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. It is good farming practice to apply 10 tonnes of cow manure for 1 acre of land. A farmer is planning to grow tomatoes in a plot of size 200 ft by 500 ft. How much manure should he buy? (Please refer to the section on Unit Conversions earlier in this chapter)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.507,
            0.85,
            0.7
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We know that 1 ton = 1000 kg, then 10 tonnes = 10,000 kg And 1 acre = 43560 sq.ft Ratio of cow manure to area of land is 10,000 : 43560 Size of plot = 200 × 500 = 100,000 sq ft. Let cow manure required be x kg Then x : 100,000 :: 10,000 : 43560 So "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\chi = \\frac{100,000 \\times 10,000}{43560} \\approx 22956.8    kg"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Hence the farmer should buy 22956.8 kg or 22.9568 tonnes of cow manure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.709,
            0.849,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. A tap takes 15 seconds to fill a mug of water. The volume of the mug is 500 mL. How much time does the same tap take to fill a bucket of water if the bucket has a 10-litre capacity?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.79,
            0.846,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence time taken to fill a 10 L bucket is 300 seconds or 5 minutes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.82,
            0.847,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. One acre of land costs ₹15,00,000. What is the cost of 2,400 square feet of the same land?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.866,
            0.426,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 1 acre = 43560 sq. ft. Cost is ₹82645 approx."
            }
          ]
        },
